WEBVTT

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.880
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:31.220
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:39.000
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:45.030
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.810
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:57.580
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:04.560
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:12.490
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:20.160
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.360
This is scary.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.620
Don't worry. I'll
protect you.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:45.600
No matter what
happens.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.560
Is that the
truth?

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:55.000
So that means you'd risk your
life to save your loved one?

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:08.410
Then you'll die
for your love.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.620
"The Great Monster Hunt"

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.430
What is this place?!

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.360
Wait for me!

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.370
Don't leave me behind!

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:23.940
Then hurry up!

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:24.870
Wait for me!

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.840
Help!

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.410
Shameful!

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.540
What on earth
was that?!

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:38.980
What's happening with
couples these days?!

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:44.710
Risking your own life for your
partner. That's true love.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:49.920
This is important especially
these days.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.890
True love.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:57.970
FILE. 40
THREE COUPLES'
DANGEROUS DATE

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.510
I'm boiling!

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.810
Nothing like being on
patrol in the summer.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.670
Na-ga-shi-me.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.820
Don't play with my head like
that! Oh, it's just you.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:21.150
Well excuse me, for being
just me and not Miyuki.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:22.530
What are you talking about?

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.930
Gee, that sure looks delicious.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:28.500
Unless I'm mistaken, that's got to be
a sweet bean pastry from Ogoya.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.370
You're not getting this.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:30.990
Jeez!

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.630
You're greedy. And to think I was going
to give you something really nice.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.600
What's with you? What are
you being so coy about?

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.840
Ta-da!

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:45.280
It's a ticket to that popular game
Amusement Wonder Square!

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.380
Oh, an amusement
park.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:51.080
Don't you know? Women
love to go there!

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:54.520
Wonder Square's a perfect place
to spend a dreamy date!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.830
No thanks,
not for me.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:02.370
Really. Poor Miyuki. Guess she'll
just have to go by herself.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.030
Hold on! Wait! What
about Kobayakawa?!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.100
She just bought
one herself.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.440
She bought
a ticket!

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:12.670
S... She did?!

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.000
I don't need one.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.070
Why not?!

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:36.190
I'll probably workout on my day off.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.200
I don't have time for
that kind of thing.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.710
After all, there's Toukairin to think of!

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.140
How about you, Aoi?

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.240
Well, it does sound kind of fun.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.700
Doesn't it?! You have good taste, madam.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.720
This has been a real learning experience.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:55.550
But how come you have so many tickets?

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.990
A friend gave me a whole bunch.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:01.720
You're selling tickets your friend gave you?

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.190
Well, look at
them all!

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.630
That's just like you!
I give up!

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.530
Have you sold
many?

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:16.500
Well, there's Nakajima, and I traded with
Miyuki for a piece of shortcake.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:19.110
Nakajima and Miyuki?!

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:33.720
Uh, Kobayakawa. Did Yoriko force you
to buy one of her tickets, too?

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:37.780
She's quite the
little hustler.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.920
What ticket? Oh,
you mean this?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:48.930
I told her I didn't want it, but it'd be
a shame to throw it away. So uh...

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:53.010
Well, are you planning
to go with anyone?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.180
Well in that case, w... w... would
you?!

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:01.980
Sure I will.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.550
On our next
day off.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.390
Together.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:08.830
Together.
Kobayakawa! Yes! Yes!

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:12.230
That's a good idea!
Great idea! Right!

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:17.560
It'd be a shame to let the
tickets go to waste!

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.370
I'll buy one! Give me one of those!

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:22.940
I knew you'd come to your senses.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:25.170
A date! How romantic!

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:28.350
If they're going on a date, they'll
definitely need my help.

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.980
Those two can't be left
to their own devices.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:37.150
And who better to follow them
than me, her trusted friend.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.360
What about you? What's your plan?

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:45.320
What? I'll just report on their progress.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.420
But I suppose I owe it to
everyone to find out...

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:51.830
...the juicy details of their
date, so I can pass it on.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.800
That means I'll
have to go!

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:55.630
Let's do it!

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.830
Come off it,
you two.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.780
What are you talking about?

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.080
Yeah, you're going to be there, too!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.310
Yeah. Right.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:18.900
Sorry to keep you.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:19.260
Not at all.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.530
I got a nosebleed.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:21.000
Are you all right?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:21.170
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:24.470
Good. The target is in sight.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.640
Everything's going as planned.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.330
Looks all right. Not bad, not bad.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.310
Why are we spying
like this?

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:35.000
Don't be so silly! In these types
of situations... Oww!

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.380
That hurts, Natsumi!

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:41.750
We're doing this for the two
of them. Right, Chief?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:47.360
People at the station have been
talking about those two.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:50.430
It's a distraction at work that can
affect the morale of the force.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.260
It must be dealt with.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.990
I am here to assess
the situation...

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.840
...and devise a plan.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.330
All right, Chief!

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:02.940
Huh.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:05.480
The target is on the move.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:06.500
Okay.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:09.580
Then we'd better
get moving, too.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:10.950
Don't let them see you.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:12.940
No, sir.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.370
Sure are lots of couples.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:28.420
Yeah.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:32.300
This is the most popular place
for couples right now.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.270
That's what Yoriko said.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.840
Is it?

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:45.720
Hey, you know what?

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:48.250
Huh? What is it?! I didn't do anything!

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.690
What's the matter?

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:52.980
You idiot! What
are you doing?!

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.390
Get with the
program!

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:58.360
Come on! Put your arm tight around her!

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.470
Calm down, Yoriko.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.520
How can I?!

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:05.100
Natsumi, go say something
to him!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:09.600
Hey. Natsumi?
Chief?

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:15.010
Ha! Not bad, if I do
say so myself.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:17.780
Aah! There they are!

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.880
Go for it, Tsujimoto!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.720
Go show them what a Bokuto
cop is made of!

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:23.510
Sir!

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.400
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.770
Natsumi!

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:35.760
Uh-oh.

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.700
Gee! You're not just playing
by yourselves, are you?

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.770
Oops. Sorry
about that.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:44.360
Just thought I might as well have
a bit of fun while we're here.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:48.510
Don't forget what we're supposed
to be doing here!

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:51.170
And what are you supposed
to be doing?

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:54.580
What else! We're here cause Miyuki
and Nakajima are here!

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.850
So? What about us?

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:03.920
Tsujimoto! Aoi! Chief!
You, too?!

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.390
Oops. Guess you
caught us.

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:20.370
Sure you're not
mad, Miyuki?

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.280
Not especially.
I'm used to it.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:25.880
Quit worrying. You'll make yourself sick.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.650
That's what I like about you, Miyuki.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:33.480
Our date! Our date
is ruined!

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.720
Here you go, Nakajima.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:39.460
I'm really sorry about this. Just when the
two of you were enjoying yourselves.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:44.530
We came along and
ruined your date.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.800
Oh well, so you
caught us.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.770
No reason to let it stop us
from having a good time!

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.110
Right, Chief?!

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:53.510
Huh? Umm, uh...

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.410
Help yourselves,
you guys.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.750
It's not much, seeing as I only made
enough for the two of us.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:01.150
Thanks, Miyuki!

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.150
Thank you! Ah!

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.890
What are you looking
at, Chief?

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.890
Uh, just this.

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.880
A new attraction?!

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:13.120
Yeah. Someone handed
this to me.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:13.700
"The Great Monster Hunt"

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:17.600
I was just wondering where this
Monster Hunt is, anyway.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.170
Hunt?!

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:22.840
Come on, you guys! Let's go to the
Monster Hunt! It'll be a riot!

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.130
Monster?

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:28.580
"The Great Monster Hunt"

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:34.650
Miyuki. Yoriko. You
guys ready?

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:35.390
Yeah.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:37.650
What's this for anyway, Natsumi?

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:42.190
It's a compact machine
gun. An MP5A4.

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:43.950
It's loaded with
paintballs.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.460
I don't know
about this.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:49.120
It's too late for that.
Let's get going.

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:56.840
Who would've thought we'd have to
get changed, just to play a game?

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.880
It sure seems
realistic.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:00.910
Welcome.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:05.310
You have entered the Great
Monster Hunt Center.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:08.720
Your mission is to hunt
down monsters.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:13.620
The field within this dome is
divided into several blocks.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:18.830
There are forests, crags,
mountains, and valleys.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:21.770
Your mission is to proceed as
you fight the monsters...

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:25.230
...and to win by destroying
their base.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:30.270
When you encounter
a monster...

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:33.040
...you may be shot.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:36.640
If you are hit, you
must play dead...

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:41.410
...and wait for instructions
until you exit the field.

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:44.410
Good luck, and
happy hunting!

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.390
Let's go!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:56.100
The target has entered
the field.

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:58.100
Who's the target?

00:12:58.270 --> 00:12:59.130
There's six
of them!

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.570
Four women,
two men.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:07.540
I wonder how many of them will
make it to the base alive.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.620
Nakajima.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:24.860
I should tell you, Miyuki's scared
of monsters and stuff like that.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:26.400
Really?

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.420
Really?
Chief, shouldn't we split up into 3 groups?

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:35.070
Yes, I suppose that might
give us an advantage.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.040
Then I'll go with
you, Chief!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:38.680
Why split up?!

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:42.540
Why split up?!
Yeah! We just have to
hit their base, right?

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:46.240
So wouldn't it be best if Miyuki
sticks with Natsumi?

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:49.880
Wait a second!
I can handle it!

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:52.390
I'm going with
Kobayakawa!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.890
Nakajima.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:57.120
Then it's settled. So that
leaves Aoi and Yoriko.

00:13:57.400 --> 00:13:59.060
What?

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.630
Us two?!

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.220
The target has split
into three groups.

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:06.600
Two couples and
two girls.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.710
Just as planned.
Start the attack.

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:12.300
And be extra hard
on the couples.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:19.170
Let's find out just how
strong their love is.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:23.450
You scared?

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:27.060
You scared?
No. I like these survival games.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:27.190
No. I like these survival games.

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:29.320
That's not what I meant.
No. I like these survival games.

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:35.430
You don't have to pretend. I know
you don't like seeing gory stuff.

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:39.590
You can hide
behind me.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.540
You got me!

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:49.510
Kobayakawa!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.810
It's awful!

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.410
Don't worry, Kobayakawa.

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:02.550
It's just some guy
who works here.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.790
I know, but it was
still awful.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.790
Oh, what a
lucky guy.

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:24.180
Oh, I'm sweating like crazy. And
we're still not at the base.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:35.190
A monster!

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:47.910
Guess I got one!

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.630
Nice shot, Yoriko.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:58.880
All right. You go around that
way. I'll go this way.

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:00.040
Roger.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:09.690
Huh?!

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:11.060
You're naive!

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.930
This is the end,
Wolfman!

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:33.550
The end!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.190
Nice going, Chief!

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:37.050
You too, Tsujimoto.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:40.850
This is good
training.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.860
Everyone's been
killed.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:49.460
No, it can't be! Well, in that
case, call everyone back!

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:50.730
What?

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:54.070
But Boss, that's against
the rules.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.040
We have no
choice!

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:58.440
However dirty the tactics
we employ...

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:02.880
...I refuse to let
them beat us!

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:10.010
Well done,
team.

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:12.610
Goes to show you're
with Bokuto Station.

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.190
I'm glad no one
got hurt.

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.660
Well? How'd it go?

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.000
What do you mean?

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.030
Hold it right there!

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:24.000
Oh no, we're surrounded!

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:30.110
That's not fair! You've
all been hit already!

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.400
Silence! We're short-staffed!

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:34.800
Prepare to die!

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:36.680
I don't know...

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:39.040
It doesn't seem like
anyone's into it.

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:43.040
Scatter on the count
of three.

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:45.650
Someone will
survive.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.530
Ready?

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:53.530
Scatter!

00:17:58.170 --> 00:17:58.770
Chief!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:17:59.960
Yoriko! Aoi!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:05.630
Aah! I'm shot! Go to...

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.310
Chief!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.740
Let's head for
the base!

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:11.780
If we hit it, we'll be the winners!

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:13.580
Yeah!

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:19.110
<i>Chief! I promise</i>
<i>we'll win!</i>

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:21.580
<i>We're counting on you.</i>

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:34.970
That's got to be it.

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:35.800
Yeah.

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.640
If we hit that and knock
it down, we'll win.

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:42.640
Not much cover up ahead, though.
How're we going to get there?

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:44.150
Leave it to me.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:47.440
They were supposed to
hold the high ground...

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:51.610
...and attack those
who approach.

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:54.750
But they've descended
first.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.830
From above, I can
handle it alone.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.530
I see.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:00.230
But...

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:02.130
Move it, you two!

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:12.910
Let's do it!

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:13.540
Right!

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:17.370
Got you!

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.640
Kobayakawa!

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:34.360
Nakajima!

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.360
Eat this!

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:42.160
I didn't think there were any
monsters left up there.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.640
Beautiful!

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:46.970
Risking your own life for
someone you love!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.610
That's the definition of true
love! I've seen it now.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.320
Where'd you pop out of?

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.980
Yeah, something weird's going on here!

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:59.350
There's an elevator for us monsters.
Special privileges, you know.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:04.100
I've had enough of this!

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:04.930
So have I!

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:06.960
Nakajima! I'll get your revenge!

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:09.120
<i>I'm not dead yet,</i>
<i>Kobayakawa.</i>

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.370
They're cheeky.

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:18.740
With that height, he has
an advantage over us.

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:22.210
There's only one monster left. We'll
just have to blast away at him.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:30.980
All my men are down. But
they still won't get me.

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:32.420
We'll see about that!

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:33.390
What?!

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.000
Natsumi!

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.260
Here goes!

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:54.610
They must be superhuman
or something.

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:58.420
All right! We did it!
All right! We did it!

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:06.020
Wow! What a rush!

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:08.190
Yeah, I had a gas!

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:10.230
I hope we can come back sometime.

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:11.860
Yeah! Let's definitely come back!

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:13.130
You'll have to do your ticket magic, Yoriko!

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:13.430
Sure, no probs!

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:16.830
What's the matter, Nakajima?

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.300
Nothing.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:23.860
Just thinking what a good team
you and Tsujimoto make.

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:25.510
Maybe better than with me.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.070
Uh-uh.

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:31.480
Next time, let's the two of us
come here alone, okay?

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:35.620
Kobayakawa.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:39.480
What's going on back there?
Hurry up, you two!

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.620
The bus'll leave
without us!

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:44.790
Yeah! We're coming!

00:21:55.740 --> 00:22:01.950
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:11.820
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:17.260
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:28.870
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:42.850
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:51.060
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.130 --> 00:22:59.700
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.940 --> 00:23:07.780
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:17.350
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:24.800
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.130
"Life or Death"

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:31.700
Last night a passenger vehicle
was attacked...

00:23:32.270 --> 00:23:37.370
...by a rogue police car
and two bikers.

00:23:38.840 --> 00:23:41.070
Attacked by rogue
police officers?!

00:23:41.350 --> 00:23:43.910
Um... that must be some
kind of mistake.

00:23:44.010 --> 00:23:49.490
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 41...

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:51.620
Why?!
